⍝ This is a sample for a menu definition.
⍝
⍝ Note that for any menu and menu item (but not separators) you MUST specify a name which is a valid
⍝ APL name. The name must be enclosed by "{" and "}". This name is used to populated a namspaces with
⍝ a reference pointing to the object in question. It is recommended to use sensefull names. 
⍝ NOTE: names must be unique for all items underneath the MenuBar object!
⍝ Seperators also get names but they are allocated automatically.
⍝
⍝ Sub-menu must be indicated by indentation, see the examplesw.
⍝
⍝ If a caption starts with a "~" character, it becomes inactive. 
⍝
⍝ If a caption starts with a "#" character, it becomes checked. I
⍝
⍝ If you specify a hint at the end of a menuitem definition this hint is shown in the statusbar when 
⍝ the user hovers with the mouse over a certain menu item.
⍝ If there is only one single field on the status bar there is no need to specify anything about it.
⍝ If there is more than one field you must specify the name of the desired status bar field control
⍝ via the optional parameters. The property name is "statusbar".
⍝
⍝ The general syntax of a menu definition is:
⍝ 1. Menu:
⍝           ↓ optional↓
⍝ [Caption] {AliasName|Groupname1|Groupname2|...}
⍝   2. Sub Menu:
⍝       [Caption] {name}
⍝ 3. One level up (after a menuitem definition owned by a submenu:
⍝   MyItem {myitem}
⍝ 4. MenuItem:
⍝        ↓ opt.↓   (or "→")          ↓mandatory↓  ↓               optional           ↓
⍝ Caption=CTRL+O : Callback-Function {AliasName} ;Hint (for a statusbar, for example!)
                         
[&File] {file}
 Open=Ctrl+O : OnTestHandler {open}        ;Specify an alias name between "{" and "}"
 New=Ctrl+N  : OnTestHandler {new} ;Opens a new document
 ~Close      : OnTestHandler   {close} ;Close a document  ⍝ Note the typo!!
 -
 &Quit=Alt+F4            : #.APLGUI.TestCases.OnTestHandler {quit}  ;Quit the program
[&Edit]                                    {edit}
 Cut=Ctrl+X              : OnTestHandler   {cut}         ;Cut an already selected piece of text to clipboard
 Copy=Ctrl+C             : OnTestHandler   {copy}        ;Copies an already selected piece of text to clipboard
 Paste=Ctrl+V            : OnTestHandler   {paste}       ;Paste the contents of the clipboard
 -
 #Display Clipboard      : OnTestHandler   {clip}        ;Opens a window+display current contents of clipboard
 [&Sub-Menus]                              {sub}
  Caption of Group1      : OnTestHandler   {gr1}         ;Displays the captions of all members of group 1
  Caption of Group2      : OnTestHandler   {gr2}         ;Displays the captions of all members of group 2
 [&Sub-Menu 1]                             {subMenu1}    ; (Alias) names of submenus must be fully qualified!
  &This                  : OnTestHandler   {this1}       ;submenu 1, this
  &That                  : OnTestHandler   {that1}       ;submenu 1, that
 -
 One Level up            : OnTestHandler   {dummy1}      ;submenu 1, that
 [&Sub Menu 1]                           
  &This                  : OnTestHandler   {SM2this2}    ;submenu 2, this
  &That                  : OnTestHandler   {SM2that2}    ;submenu 2, that
  T&This                 : OnTestHandler   {SM2this3}    ;submenu 2, this
 [&Sub-Menu level 2]                       {SM2SubSub}
  &Level 2               : OnTestHandler   {level2}      ;sub menu of a sub menu
[&Help]                                    {helpMenu}
 Help=F1                 : OnTestHandler   {help}       
 -
 About                   : OnTestHandler   {about}       ;Copyright, originator and homepage 
